    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2_1_1Http">api::v2::Http</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Maps caught exceptions to the HTTP status reported to API clients. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides one small helper, statusForException, that looks at an exception which was caught and decides which HTTP status code the client should receive. A &quot;database busy&quot; problem maps to 503 (try again later); every other problem maps to 500 (generic server error). The function is inline and header-only, so there is no separate .cpp file and no linking needed.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: When a controller fails while handling a request it must still send an HTTP answer. The CRITICALMESSAGERESPONSE macro (in <ref refid="global_8hpp" kindref="compound">global.hpp</ref>) calls this helper to choose that answer&apos;s status. Doing the choice in one place keeps every error response consistent: clients always get 503 specifically when the database was too busy, and 500 for anything else. Without it, each catch block would have to repeat the classification logic.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Exceptions in C++: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/exception">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/exception</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>dynamic_cast: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/dynamic_cast">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/dynamic_cast</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>inline functions: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/inline">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/inline</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
